---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, fullAddress } from '../data/site';
const effective = 'November 1, 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description="Terms that apply to Tek Media Group repair services and use of this website.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Terms of service</h1><p>Effective {effective}</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p>
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") apply to repair and service work performed by {site.name} ("we," "us," "our")
      and to your use of this website. By requesting service, delivering equipment to us, or using this website, you
      agree to these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Estimates and authorization</h2>
    <p>
      Estimates are free, and we do not charge a diagnosis fee on out-of-warranty products. We will give you a written
      estimate and will not perform work or charge for parts or labor beyond the estimate without your authorization.
      If we find that more work is needed, we will contact you for approval first. Estimates are valid for 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Warranty repairs</h2>
    <p>
      Manufacturer warranty repairs are performed under the manufacturer's terms. You may need to provide proof of
      purchase. If the manufacturer determines that a product is not covered, we will give you an estimate before
      doing any work.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Parts and repair warranty</h2>
    <p>
      Parts and labor are covered by the warranty stated on your invoice. The warranty covers the specific repair
      performed and does not cover unrelated failures, physical or liquid damage, misuse, or repairs by others after
      the equipment leaves our shop. Replaced parts may be discarded unless you ask for them back when you approve the
      estimate. We may use new, refurbished, or equivalent parts as permitted by law; the invoice will say so.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Shipping</h2>
    <p>
      If you ship equipment to us, pack it securely, remove accessories, media and memory cards, and include your ticket
      number. You are responsible for shipping costs and for insuring the shipment for its full value; we are not
      responsible for damage or loss in transit to us. Return shipping is charged as shown on your invoice.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      Repair work can result in loss of stored data. Back up anything you want to keep before service. We are not
      responsible for loss of data, software, settings or media stored on or inserted in your equipment.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Payment</h2>
    <p>
      Payment is due when the repair is complete and before equipment is released or shipped back. We accept the payment
      methods listed on our website and invoices. Unpaid balances may be subject to collection as permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Pickup and unclaimed equipment</h2>
    <p>
      Please collect or arrange return of your equipment within 30 days after we notify you that it is ready or that
      you declined the estimate. Equipment that is not claimed after notice may be treated as abandoned and disposed of
      or sold to cover charges, as permitted by California law, including written notice to you before any sale.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability for any claim arising from our services is limited to
      the amount you paid for the service giving rise to the claim. We are not liable for indirect, incidental,
      consequential or lost-profit damages, including production downtime or lost data. Nothing in these Terms limits
      rights you have under California or federal law that cannot be waived.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Communications</h2>
    <p>
      By giving us your email address or phone number, you agree that we may contact you about your service. We will
      send marketing messages only as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, and you can opt out at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Use of this website</h2>
    <p>
      Website content is for general information and may change without notice. Prices, services and turnaround times
      shown are estimates and are not guaranteed. Do not misuse the website, interfere with its operation, or attempt to
      access accounts or data that are not yours. All content, logos and design are owned by {site.name} or used with
      permission. Product and brand names belong to their respective owners and are used only to describe equipment we
      service; their use does not imply endorsement unless stated.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Privacy</h2>
    <p>Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle personal information and is part of these Terms.</p>

    <h2>12. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California and applicable U.S. federal law. Before filing a
      claim, please contact us so we can try to resolve it informally. Any dispute that is not resolved will be heard in
      the state or federal courts located in Los Angeles County, California, or in small claims court where eligible.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these Terms. The version posted on this page on the date you request service applies to that service.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name}<br />{fullAddress}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
      Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
    </p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
